WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.770
Leah: Listening does not always get
classed as a communication skill,

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.529
but it can be one of the most
important skills, which can have a

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:11.379
major impact on job effectiveness
and relationships with others.

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:15.970
We use listening to obtain
information and to learn, so that

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:20.640
we can process and understand that
information and utilise our skills

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.590
in interpreting and acting on it.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.590
However, we don’t always hear
everything that is be said to us

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.470
especially if we are distracted.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.759
Jack: The way to improve our listening
skills is by ‘active listening’ where

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.080
a conscious effort is made to take
on board the complete message that

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.210
is being communicated, as well as
the words that the person is saying.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:44.007
It is a way of listening that
keeps a person involved with their

00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:45.759
conversation partner in a positive way.

00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:49.556
In order to practice ‘active listening’
a person needs to pay careful attention

00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:53.645
to what is being said making the
other person feel that they are being

00:00:53.645 --> 00:00:56.857
listened to and not get distracted
by anything else around them.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.000
They must also keep focussed
on what is being said without

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.790
getting bored or losing interest.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.080
Leah: ‘Active listening’ also serves the
purpose of earning the trust of others

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.360
and having the opportunity to offer
support and empathy to the speaker.

00:01:10.809 --> 00:01:14.350
‘Active listening’ is particularly
important when a person is

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.960
in a supervisory position or
interacting with colleagues.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.570
It helps with understanding problems
and collaboration on projects.

